G2270.d:
ἡσυχάζω
 [in LXX chiefly for שָׁקַט ;]
to be still;
 __(a) to rest from labour: Luk.23:56;
 __(b) to live quietly: 1Th.4:11;
 __(with) to be silent: Luk.14:3, Act.11:18 21:14 (cf. Job.32:7, Neh.5:8).†
 SYN.: σιγάω (which see), σιωπάω (AS)

G3674.d:
ὁμοῦ
 adv. (ὁμός),
together;
 __(a) prop., of place: Jhn.21:2, Act.2:1;
 __(b) without idea of place: Jhn.4:36 20:4.†
 (AS)

G3438.d:
μονή, -ῆς, ἡ
 (μένω), [in LXX: 1Ma.7:38 * ;]
__1. in cl.,
 __(a) a staying, abiding;
 __(b) continuance (LXX, 1 with)
 __2. In late Gk.,
 __(a) a statson (Paus.);
 __(b) an abode: Jhn.14:2, 23;
 __(with) a monastery (cf. MM, iii, xvi; so in MGr.).†
 (AS)

G1106.d:
γνώμη, -ης, ἡ
 (γιγνώσκω), [in LXX: Da TH 2:15 (דָּת), Ps 82(83):3 (סוֹד), elsewhere, chiefly II Es, for טְעֵם ;]
 __1. a means of knowing, a token (Theogn.).
 __2. In Attic writers, the mind, its operations and results (see Edwards, Lex., App., A);
__(a) mind, understanding;
 __(b) purpose, intention: Act.20:3;
 __(with) judgment, opinion: 1Co.1:10, Rev.17:13;
 __(d) counsel, advice: 1Co.7:25, 40 2Co.8:10, Phm 14;
 __(e) royal purpose, decree (as in Da, I and II Es): Rev.17:17 (Cremer, 671).
 † (AS)

G0862.d:
ἄ-φθαρτος, -ον
 (φθείρω), [in LXX: Wis.12:1 18:4 * ;]
imperishable, immortal;
 __(a) of things: 1Co.9:25, 1Pe.1:4 1:23 3:4;
 __(b) of persons: of men, 1Co.15:52; of God, Rom.1:23, 1Ti.1:17 (MM, see word).†
 (AS)

G1506.d:
εἰλικρινής, -ές,
 [in LXX: Wi 72^ kB * ;]
unalloyed, pure (Lat. sincerus; see DCG, ii, 635a);
__(a) of unmixed substances;
 __(b) of abstract ideas;
 __(with) of ethical purity: Php.1:10, 2Pe.3:1.†
 SYN.: ἁγνός (which see), καθαρός, cf. Tr., Syn.: §lxxxv; DB, iv, 176a; Cremer, 378; Westc. on 1Jn.3:3. (AS)
